   "wanted": "A positive mechanical nut capture (an inward lip/ridge over the nut) so retention does not depend on press-fit friction",
   "blocked_by": "The constraint that it be one printed piece with the nut pressed in by hand and no glue: a rigid M5 hex nut (8.0 across flats, 9.24 across corners) cannot pass an opening that blocks it, and it has no room to tilt/rotate inside the socket, so an axial capture lip would have to be sprung past elastically; PLA in a 6 mm-thick section would scrape or crack rather than spring. A radial insert-and-close channel needs two pieces",
   "why": "A captured nut is the only retention that is completely independent of how the printer sizes the hex socket"
  }
